<title>UK: NWE oil products stronger with crude.</title>
<headline>NWE oil products stronger with crude.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>NWE oil products firmed with crude on Wednesday, traders said.</p>
<p>Gasoline supply remained tight, especially for high octane grades.</p>
<p>Naphtha swaps lifted slightly, but markets were quiet after most prompt demand was covered.</p>
<p>Gas oil rose with IPE futures and spot premiums were steady, but diesel maintained a huge premium to heating oil.</p>
<p>Fuel oil took support from stronger crude although trade was becalmed.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 8145</p>
</text>
